# Wave W17-AA (Route 219): bright rock — jetty-foot rock: a warm grey boulder standing in the lane’s bright shallows, foam collar at its base, the south sea road’s scattered footing stones (design: the lane runs off Shingle beach through bright water). The baked water is the shipped sea entire — the lane’s brightness is carried by the boulder’s warm sunlit face, never by a mismatched water square. Route 219’s own rock — split from its twin Route 220’s swell rock by face entire (warm sunlit vs swell-shadow dark) and from Route 218’s footing rock by office: this stone stands alone in a lane, that one carries a causeway.
